iperf3 servers listening on ports 5201, 5202, 5203, 5204, 5205, 5206
guests reachable with iperf3: V1=tenant1, V2=tenant5, A=tenant2, B=tenant3, C=tenant4, D=tenant6; ping on tenant5
SCENARIO steady4 (exp41 mixed traffic): flooder A (tenant2) t=0-28 s TCP bulk (2 streams), flooder B (tenant3) t=6-34 s UDP flood -b 6G (1 stream), flooder C (tenant4) t=12-40 s bursty TCP 2 s on / 2 s off (2 streams), flooder D (tenant6) t=18-40 s TCP bulk (8 streams); all scheduled 18-28 s (Jain / min_ovl / high-cap window, as exp40)
BURSTS C: 7 separate iperf3 -t 2 runs, all launched at slot start with sleep 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 36 s; own-window means over its envelope 12-40 s (28 s, off phases included); vfrot/vffair see it go inactive between bursts (offered < 50 Mbit/s) and, unchanged from exp40, reset the delivered counters each time all four become active again
CONFIGS: vfrot 0.8_1_2_0.94 (beta 0.8, add 1, T 2, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000), vffair 0.8_1_2_0.94_F0.25 (beta 0.8, add 1, T 2, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000, floor 0.25), lqr 79_4, lqr 85_4, lqr 90_4, static 2500 (10 Gbit/s total), static 3500 (14 Gbit/s total)
REFERENCE CONFIG for the paired summary: vfrot 0.8_1_2_0.94 (identical to exp39/exp40 vfrot)
TOKEN BUCKET: all modes use the same xdp_limit.o on every flooder interface, burst 5 ms at the cap rate; victim interfaces never limited (counter only)
VICTIMS: V1 = tenant1 10.10.0.11 port 5201 9 Gbit/s, V2 = tenant5 10.10.0.15 port 5205 2 Gbit/s, one TCP stream each, constant for [0,40) s (launched together 0.5 s after the flooders); slo_ok per victim = fraction of its 39 1 s windows >= 95% of its own per-repeat reference; slo_ok_worst = the smaller of the two
LATENCY: tenant5 pings 10.10.0.1 every 0.2 s during each run (200 probes) and each reference run; reference p99 = p99 of all received reference replies of the repeat (2 x 100 probes; loss > 5% refuses); per run: p50/p99 over received replies, loss %; slo_ok_v2_rtt = 1 iff the run's p99 <= max(2 x reference p99, 2 ms) AND loss <= 1% (lost pings fail the RTT SLO only through loss > 1%, i.e. more than 2 of 200 probes); slo_ok_worst_with_rtt = min(ok_v1, ok_v2) x slo_ok_v2_rtt; the controllers never see the RTT
